# Saving through the real keys: play a little (walk off the square, lay a fire),
# save to a slot from the slate's saves app, leave for the title, continue, and the
# world that comes back is the one that was saved.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/saves.tour --seed=1 --hour=10 --weather=clear:0 --give=driftwood:6,stone:4
# (A tour saves under user://tool-saves/<tour name>, never over a player's games
# nor into the folder of another tour run beside it.)
coast calm
walk -1,0 2.2
# Off the square and standing on open turf: a fire needs ground with nothing on
# it, and which tile two seconds west of a spawn is has changed with worldgen
# more than once. `ground` asks the world where its turf is instead of guessing.
ground grass
wait 0.4
tap use
wait 0.4
tap use
await made 3
wait 0.5
shot 01-played
# Long enough for the lines about the fire to fade: the frame to match has no words on it.
wait 5
shot 02-before
# The fire laid is in reach where the game is saved.
await station:fire 1
tap pause
wait 0.5
choose saves
tap use
await app:saves 2
wait 0.3
shot 03-save-page with app:saves
# An empty slot is written at once; one that holds a game (an earlier run's) asks
# first, and the second press writes over it.
try 2
tap use
await saved 1.5
end
wait 0.3
shot 04-saved
tap pause
wait 0.4
choose title
tap use
# Leaving writes the autosave, so to the title never throws play away.
await saved 2
await title 30
wait 0.5
shot 05-title
# The title reads its keys as key events. New game would write over that autosave,
# so it asks once more; going back up to Continue forgets the question.
key move_down
key use
wait 0.4
shot 05b-new-asks
key move_up
# Continue is the newest save: the autosave made on leaving, the game as it was saved.
key use
await game 30
coast calm
# The place name letters itself on arrival and fades; then the world as it was saved.
wait 6
shot 06-after
# The same place, light and slate. Six world minutes pass between the two —
# saving, leaving to the title, and coming back through Continue — and the save
# carries the clock, so the sun has moved a little in every pixel of both; a
# village lives, so its people and its dogs have walked; and the flame of the
# fire is never still. That is what these tolerances hold room for, and nothing
# else: the crop below is round the player and the fire they laid, and losing
# the fire out of it takes the difference well past its allowance.
# The crop's allowance was 0.024, tuned when `ground grass` left the player in
# the village square with the fire half out of frame. It is now laid on open turf
# with the flame square in the middle of the crop, which is the most restless
# thing in the picture — measured over three runs at this staging: whole frame
# 0.0229 / 0.0236 / 0.0275, crop 0.0250 / 0.0255 / 0.0257. A spread of 0.0007
# with the fire THERE, against a tolerance that has to be well under what losing
# it costs; 0.030 keeps the guard and stops it failing on the flame it is
# watching.
same 02-before 06-after 0.032
same 02-before 06-after 0.030 440,220,440,280
await station:fire 1
# Load from home's saves app too (right turns it to loading): the autosave and the
# three slots, and slot 1 taken up again.
walk 1,0 1
tap pause
wait 0.5
choose saves
tap use
await app:saves 2
tap move_right
wait 0.3
choose slot_1
wait 0.3
shot 07-load-page with app:saves
tap use
await game 30
coast calm
wait 6
shot 08-loaded
# Further from the save than 06 was: this one went out through home's saves app
# and back, so a few more world minutes of sun are in it (same reasons as above).
same 02-before 08-loaded 0.036
same 02-before 08-loaded 0.028 440,220,440,280
await station:fire 1
